<p>In the latest turn, Iran said it had rejected or responded negatively to a 15-point US ceasefire proposal and instead set out its own conditions for ending nearly four weeks of war, while President Trump and the White House insisted messages and peace efforts were still continuing. Several reports said Tehran&#x27;s position included demands such as reparations and terms tied to the Strait of Hormuz, though accounts differed on whether Iran had fully rejected talks or was still reviewing the proposal through intermediaries. Fighting continued as diplomacy remained uncertain. Iran launched more attacks on Israel and on Gulf locations, with reports of strikes affecting Kuwait International Airport and attacks aimed at US-linked sites in Kuwait, Jordan and Bahrain, while Israel carried out airstrikes on Tehran and the United States sent more forces to the region. Even so, several sources pointed to a narrow opening for de-escalation: indirect messages were still moving, mediators were trying to arrange a direct meeting, and China said it saw a &quot;glimmer of hope&quot; for negotiations.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/0TOC4LHyHskyYchRfL4MKc0zpMwUs1M_idEk6XkwH1fgmxHzahgsDo4Xia9iAN-993MO0FsNU4Wkt0Ztd_0c3VsF1iv8u_Tt6KwlnPIBi5DGdO7HCXSkt7XlY8b2nUH-cNBNIBLGXcTvqn4eKXs4-y3oledpBkrb4Anp0qlG8t4haPkbdilStNgc' alt='Scene linked to reporting on Iran rejecting a US proposal to end the war.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Trump framing: President Trump said Iran wanted a deal &quot;so badly&quot; and argued its public denials were meant to save face because negotiators feared retaliation at home.</li><li>Ceasefire dilemma: Reporting suggested Tehran was wary of a simple pause in fighting, fearing Washington and Israel could use any temporary truce to regroup before strikes resumed.</li><li>Mediator warning: Countries trying to broker contact were said to be pushing for a direct US-Iran meeting, which some described as a last chance to prevent a broader escalation.</li><li>Strategic tension: The New York Times reported that Israel was concerned a war-ending deal could come before it had dismantled Iran&#x27;s weapons programs, helping explain why military pressure continued alongside diplomacy.</li></ul><blockquote>President Trump does not bluff and he is prepared to unleash hell. Iran should not miscalculate again. - Karoline Leavitt</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian government: Araghchi drew a line between receiving a US proposal and entering negotiations, saying Tehran could review what Washington sent while still refusing direct talks to wind down the war. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-says-it-is-reviewing-a-us-ceasefire-plan-but-no-talks/article70786754.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>White House: Karoline Leavitt cast US outreach as coercive diplomacy, saying contacts were continuing while warning Iran not to mistake talks for reduced military pressure. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-israel-tehran-mocks-us-warns-against-ground-invasion/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Chinese government: Wang Yi framed the moment as mutual signaling rather than a breakthrough, saying both Washington and Tehran appeared to be leaving at least a small diplomatic opening. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/26/iran-war-live-updates-trump-deal-us-military-strikes-israel-lebanon-hezbollah'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Israeli leadership: Israeli officials were reported to see timing as the key risk, fearing that an early ceasefire could freeze the battlefield before Israel reached its goal of dismantling Iran&#x27;s weapons programs. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/25/world/iran-war-trump-oil-news'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Mediating countries: Intermediaries were described as trying to move the process from message-passing to an actual face-to-face US-Iran meeting, which some cast as the last viable off-ramp. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-25/iran-rejects-trumps-15-point-proposal-to-end-the-war.html'>El País</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3347913/iran-rejects-us-ceasefire-plan-issues-own-demands-strikes-land-across-middle-east'>Iran rejects US ceasefire plan, has own demands to end fighting</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/26/trump-insists-iran-badly-wants-a-deal-with-the-us-after-tehran-dismisses-his-ceasefire-pro'>Trump insists Iran &#x27;badly&#x27; wants deal with the US after Tehran dismisses his ceasefire proposal</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/03/26/bncv-m26.html'>White House threatens to “unleash hell” against Iran, as US surges troops to Middle East</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-israel-tehran-mocks-us-warns-against-ground-invasion/'>White House says Trump will &quot;unleash hell&quot; if Iran doesn&#x27;t make deal</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly9nz5vyz4o'>What are the US and Iran&#x27;s proposals for peace?</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iran-says-it-reviewing-us-ceasefire-plan-no-talks-trump-says-tehran-leaders-want'>Iran says it is reviewing a US ceasefire plan but no talks; Trump says Tehran leaders want a deal</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/26/iran-war-live-updates-trump-deal-us-military-strikes-israel-lebanon-hezbollah'>Middle East crisis live: Trump insists Iran wants a deal despite initial rejection; China sees ‘glimmer of hope’ for talks</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-says-it-is-reviewing-a-us-ceasefire-plan-but-no-talks/article70786754.ece'>Iran says it is reviewing a U.S. ceasefire plan but no talks</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/20